Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: idle-status-screen
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3,
         kmscon,
         tmux,
         kbd,
         systemd,
         fonts-dejavu-core
Recommends: btop
Suggests: htop, atop, sddm
Description: show system status (btop) while the login screen is idle
 When nobody is logged in graphically and there is no keyboard, mouse or
 touchscreen input for a while, the display switches from the login screen
 (SDDM or another display manager greeter) to a virtual terminal showing a
 system monitor such as btop, htop, atop or top. Any input switches back to
 the login screen.
 .
 The monitor runs from boot in a tmux session, so graphs keep their history,
 and is shown read-only through kmscon (TrueType fonts with Braille glyphs,
 truecolor). X server screen blanking and DPMS are disabled.
